Tables 1.1 to 1.3 present a comparative analysis of five existing digital reading systems 
relevant to the development of TaraBasa AI. The comparison matrix provides a structured overview 
of Google Read Along, Lexia Core5 Reading, Raz-Kids, Read with Ello, and Amira Learning by 
examining their key features, limitations, platform details, support mechanisms, and monetization 

26
schemes. This comparison identifies the capabilities and limitations of existing reading 
technologies and establishes the basis for the design and development of TaraBasa AI.
TaraBasa AI shares several features with the reviewed systems. Similar to Google Read 
Along, Read with Ello, and Amira Learning, it incorporates AI-powered reading assessment and 
speech recognition to evaluate learners' oral reading and provide immediate feedback. Like Lexia 
Core5 Reading, Read with Ello, and Amira Learning, TaraBasa AI includes adaptive learning 
activities that personalize instruction based on learner performance. It also incorporates gamified 
reading activities, a feature found in Google Read Along, Lexia Core5 Reading, Raz-Kids, and 
Read with Ello, to promote learner engagement and motivation. In addition, TaraBasa AI provides 
a teacher dashboard and progress analytics, similar to Lexia Core5 Reading, Raz-Kids, and Amira 
Learning, enabling teachers to monitor learner performance and make informed instructional 
decisions.
Despite these similarities, TaraBasa AI offers several features that distinguish it from the 
reviewed systems. Unlike the existing applications, TaraBasa AI integrates AI reading 
recommendations and AI intervention recommendations that assist teachers in selecting appropriate 
reading activities and interventions based on learner performance. It also includes a Personal Word 
Bank that records mastered vocabulary to reinforce reading development over time. Furthermore, 
TaraBasa AI is the only system among those reviewed that provides parent monitoring with SMS 
notifications, allowing parents to receive timely updates on their child's reading progress and 
intervention activities. By combining AI-powered reading assessment, speech recognition, adaptive 
learning, AI-driven recommendations, gamified learning, teacher and parent monitoring, learner 
analytics, and a personal vocabulary feature within a single platform, TaraBasa AI delivers a more 
comprehensive and practical reading intervention system than the existing applications.

