Table 2 presents a comparative evaluation of TaraBasa AI alongside existing digital 
reading systems: Google Read Along, Lexia Core5 Reading, Raz-Kids, Read with Ello, and Amira 

28
Learning. While each platform supports particular aspects of literacy instruction, such as AIpowered reading assessment, speech recognition, adaptive learning, gamified reading activities, 
and learner progress monitoring, TaraBasa AI stands out by integrating these capabilities into a 
single platform specifically designed for Philippine public elementary schools. Google Read Along 
supports AI-powered oral reading practice through speech recognition and pronunciation feedback 
but provides limited intervention planning and parent involvement. Lexia Core5 Reading 
emphasizes adaptive learning, teacher monitoring, and learner analytics but functions as a general 
literacy platform rather than a localized intervention system. Raz-Kids provides digital reading 
resources, gamified activities, and progress monitoring but does not incorporate artificial 
intelligence or speech recognition. Read with Ello combines AI-powered reading assessment with 
personalized reading support but lacks intervention planning and parent monitoring features. Amira 
Learning offers comprehensive AI-powered assessment, speech recognition, adaptive instruction, 
and teacher analytics but is designed primarily for English-speaking educational settings and is not 
aligned with Phil-IRI processes or the MATATAG Curriculum. In contrast, TaraBasa AI uniquely 
integrates AI-powered reading assessment, speech recognition, AI pronunciation coaching, 
adaptive learning activities, an AI Reading Intervention Planner, AI Intervention Identification, a 
Personal Word Bank, gamified reading activities, teacher and parent dashboards with SMS 
notifications, learner progress analytics, and Philippine curriculum alignment within a unified 
platform. By combining these features into one system, TaraBasa AI provides a more 
comprehensive, localized, and practical solution for supporting reading intervention among Grade 
1 to Grade 3 learners in Philippine public elementary schools.

29
CHAPTER III
RESEARCH METHODOLOGY
This chapter presents the research methodology adopted in the development of TaraBasa 
AI. It discusses the software engineering methodology applied throughout the study, including the 
planning and initiation phase, Business Model Canvas, program workflow, validation board (Stage 
1 and Stage 2), and Gantt chart. The chapter also covers the analysis and design phase, which 
includes the use case diagram, user interface design, storyboard, database design, and network 
design, together with the proposed system model and topology. In addition, it describes the 
development and construction phase by presenting the technology stack, software and hardware 
specifications, program specifications, and the different modules integrated into the proposed 
system. These components served as the foundation for the systematic design, development, 
implementation, and evaluation of TaraBasa AI.
Software Engineering Methodology
The development process for TaraBasa AI will be based on the Agile methodology because 
of its iterative and flexible approach, which supports continuous system improvement and the 
timely delivery of functional features. Since TaraBasa AI is designed to address the English reading 
needs of Grade 1 to Grade 3 learners while accommodating feedback from teachers and parents, 
the Agile methodology enables the development team to adapt efficiently to user requirements 
throughout the project. Its emphasis on collaboration, continuous feedback, and incremental 
development provides a structured framework that minimizes development risks and ensures that 
the proposed system meets the needs of its intended users.
Figure 2. Agile Methodology
The researchers will utilize the iterative nature of Agile to monitor development progress, 
evaluate completed features, and ensure that the project remains aligned with its planned schedule. 
This methodology is appropriate for TaraBasa AI because the system integrates multiple 

30
components, including AI-powered reading assessment, speech recognition, adaptive learning 
activities, gamified reading exercises, learner progress monitoring, teacher and parent dashboards, 
and SMS notifications. The flexibility of Agile allows each development sprint to produce a 
functional system increment that can be evaluated and refined based on feedback from teachers, 
parents, and selected users. This approach reduces the need for extensive revisions during the later 
stages of development and ensures that the system remains responsive to educational needs.
Planning Phase. The researchers will gather and analyze the requirements for TaraBasa 
AI through interviews, surveys, and consultations with teachers and other stakeholders. This phase 
involves identifying the challenges encountered in English reading instruction, learner assessment, 
and progress monitoring to establish the functional and non-functional requirements of the 
proposed system. The information collected will serve as the basis for preparing the project scope, 
user requirements, and development plan.
Design Phase. The researchers will design the overall architecture of TaraBasa AI based 
on the identified requirements. This phase includes designing the AI-powered reading assessment 
process, adaptive learning workflow, speech recognition integration, teacher and parent 
dashboards, database structure, and user interface. Storyboards, use case diagrams, database 
models, and other design documents will also be prepared to provide a clear guide for system 
development.
Development Phase. During this phase, the researchers will convert the approved system 
design into a functional application by developing the various modules of TaraBasa AI. This 
includes implementing the AI-assisted reading assessment, adaptive learning activities, gamified 
reading exercises, learner monitoring features, teacher and parent dashboards, and SMS notification 
functionality. Unit testing will be conducted throughout development to ensure that each module 
performs according to the specified requirements.
Testing Phase. Once the system modules have been completed, comprehensive testing will 
be conducted to verify the functionality, reliability, and usability of TaraBasa AI. Functional 
testing, integration testing, performance testing, and usability testing will be performed to identify 
and resolve any errors or inconsistencies. Feedback from selected teachers and users will also be 
gathered to further improve the quality and effectiveness of the proposed system before 
deployment.
Deployment Phase. After successful testing, TaraBasa AI will be deployed to its intended 
web-based environment. This phase includes configuring the hosting environment, deploying the 
application, validating the system's core functionalities, and preparing user guides or 
documentation to assist teachers, parents, and learners in using the system effectively.

31
Review Phase. Following deployment, the researchers will evaluate the overall 
performance of TaraBasa AI by collecting feedback from its intended users. User responses, system 
performance, and identified issues will be analyzed to determine possible enhancements and future 
improvements. The results of the evaluation will serve as the basis for refining the system in 
succeeding development iterations while ensuring that all modifications are properly documented.
