Planning/Conception-Initiation Phase 
During this phase, the objectives, scope, and system requirements of the proposed study 
will be identified and clearly defined. This includes developing a Business Model Canvas to 
evaluate the overall concept of TaraBasa AI, a program workflow to illustrate the interactions of 
learners, teachers, parents, and administrators with the system, and a validation board to identify 
the existing challenges in English reading intervention and determine the proposed solution. 
Furthermore, a Gantt chart will be prepared to present the project's activities and corresponding 
development timeline, while a functional decomposition diagram will be created to divide the major 
system processes into smaller and more manageable functions that will guide the design and 
development of the proposed system.
Business Model Canvas 
The Business Model Canvas (BMC) enables the researchers to visualize and evaluate the 
overall concept of TaraBasa AI. By examining its Key Partners, Key Activities, Value Propositions, 
Customer Relationships, Customer Segments, Key Resources, Channels, Cost Structure, and 
Revenue Streams, the researchers can gain a comprehensive understanding of the proposed 

37
system's value and feasibility. This tool also helps identify the strengths, opportunities, and areas 
for improvement of the proposed system, allowing the researchers to make informed decisions 
throughout the design, development, and implementation of TaraBasa AI.
