Support
“TaraBasa AI,” an AI-powered mobile and web platform for adaptive reading assessment 
and intervention, is developed using a structured technology stack suited to the low-resource 
conditions of Philippine public elementary schools. The mobile application is built using Android 
Studio, leveraging Kotlin for modern Android development and Android Material Design 
principles for a clean, child-friendly interface suitable for Grade 1 to Grade 3 learners on lowspecification devices. The AI reading assessment functionality is powered by the Google Cloud 
Speech-to-Text API, which transcribes each learner's oral reading for comparison against the 
expected passage text, allowing the system's own rule-based logic to compute accuracy and reading 
speed without requiring the research team to train a speech recognition model from scratch.
The backend infrastructure relies on an Apache server managed through XAMPP, with 
PHP handling server-side logic and a MySQL database storing all user accounts, learner records, 
reading passages, and session results. Communication between the mobile application, web 
dashboard, and database is handled through RESTful APIs. Parent communication is supported 
through an SMS Gateway API, dispatching both immediate alerts and routine weekly summaries 
regardless of whether the parent owns a smartphone or a basic mobile phone.
The web component of “TaraBasa AI,” used for the Teacher Dashboard, Parent Dashboard, 
and Admin Panel, is built with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, styled using Bootstrap for responsive, 
mobile-friendly layouts. Looking ahead, future development includes expanding support to the iOS 
platform, adding full Bisaya voice recognition support, and introducing an offline mode to better 
serve schools with limited or inconsistent internet connectivity.

128
Software Specification
This section presents the software that will be used, including the operating system, 
programming languages for both the front-end and back-end of the application, platforms, and 
database requirements needed to develop the entire “TaraBasa AI” system. It functions as a 
blueprint that the researchers must follow to develop the program correctly. Before the construction 
process can commence, the researchers must establish an accurate and complete software 
specification.
