Speech Recognition ServiceGoogle Cloud Speech-to-Text API
SMS Gateway Semaphore SMS API (or equivalent Philippine SMS gateway)
Table 24 outlines the software specification for developing the “TaraBasa AI” platform. 
The researchers chose Windows for development machines and Android OS version 8.0 and above 
for mobile compatibility, reflecting the low-specification Android devices commonly available in 
Philippine public elementary schools. Visual Studio Code and Android Studio serve as the primary 
text editors and IDEs, with PHP, Kotlin, and JavaScript as the programming languages used across 
the web backend, Android application, and client-side interactivity, respectively. Supported web 
browsers include Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge, and Mozilla Firefox. MySQL, managed 
through the XAMPP/Apache server stack, serves as the database, while Bootstrap is used for 
responsive web design across the Teacher, Parent, and Admin dashboards. The Google Cloud 
Speech-to-Text API and a Philippine SMS gateway service round out the specification, supporting 
the platform's core AI assessment and parent communication features respectively.

129
Hardware Specification 
This section provides a detailed description of the hardware requirements needed for the 
system. It outlines the specifications, requirements, and limitations of each hardware component 
necessary to support the development, deployment, and operation of the proposed system.
Table 25
HARDWARE SPECIFICATIONS
PC
CPU
64-bit or 32-bit support
2.5GHz or faster processor
Intel i5 10th Gen+ or AMD Ryzen 5 3000 series or higher
Memory At least 8 GB RAM or above
Storage 10 GB Available space or more
GPU Integrated or Dedicated Graphics
Intel UHD Graphics or AMD Graphics or Nvidia Graphics
Mobile
CPU Octa Core or more
2.0 GHz or faster processor
Memory At least 4 GB RAM or above
Storage 6 GB available space or more
Camera 12MP or higher
Table 25 outlines the hardware specifications for TaraBasa AI, detailing the minimum 
requirements for both personal computers (PCs) and Android mobile devices to ensure efficient 
system development and operation. For PC development, the recommended specifications include 
a 64-bit processor with a minimum clock speed of 2.5 GHz, such as an Intel Core i5 (10th 
Generation) or AMD Ryzen 5 processor and above. The system also requires at least 8 GB of RAM, 
a minimum of 10 GB of available storage, and integrated or dedicated graphics to support web 
development and system management. For Android mobile devices, the recommended 
specifications include an octa-core processor with a minimum clock speed of 2.0 GHz, at least 4 
GB of RAM, and 6 GB of available storage. A built-in microphone is also required to support the 
application's AI-powered speech recognition and pronunciation assessment features. These 

130
specifications are intended to ensure reliable performance and compatibility across both the web 
and Android platforms of TaraBasa AI.
Program Specification 
The program specification defines the expected functionalities and objectives of TaraBasa 
AI, serving as a guide throughout the system development process. It organizes the system into its 
major functional modules, allowing the researchers to systematically design, develop, and 
implement each component while ensuring that all system requirements and features are effectively 
integrated.
